      },
      "blocks": {
        "q1": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I wear them for Hajj or Umrah?",
            "answer": "<p>A lot of people buy them for pilgrimage, where facilities are shared and there’s nowhere to dry anything. On the separate question of footwear restrictions in ihram, ask a scholar — that isn’t a question we should be answering.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q2": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can children use them for wudu?",
            "answer": "<p>Our sizes start at UK 3, so they fit older children. On whether and from what age masah applies for a child, ask a scholar rather than a sock company.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Are they suitable for use at the mosque?",
            "answer": "<p>There’s no reason they wouldn’t be. The practical reason people buy them is for the places where wudu is harder — offices, sites, airports, universities — rather than a mosque with proper facilities.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q4": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do you sell a separate wudu version?",
            "answer": "<p>No. It’s the same sock, the same waterproof layer and the same build whichever page you buy it from, at the same price. There’s no wudu edition and no wudu premium.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q5": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What happens if water gets inside them during wudu?",
            "answer": "<p>This is covered in the sources and it’s a point we’ve deliberately not paraphrased, because getting it approximately right would be worse than not answering.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q6": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Who has reviewed these socks?",
            "answer": "<p>Shaykh Mufti Saiful Islam of the JKN Institute in Bradford, and Mufti Amjad Mohammed of Dār al-ʿUlūm al-Zaytuniyya, also in Bradford.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "q1",
        "q2",
